{
  "name": "Unarmed Fighting",
  "type": "feat",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Your Unarmed Strikes can deal bludgeoning damage equal to 1d6 + your Strength modifier on a hit. If you aren't wielding any weapons or a shield when you make the Attack Roll, the d6 becomes a d8.</p><p>At the start of each of your turns, you can deal 1d4 bludgeoning damage to one creature Grappled by you.</p><p>If you have another feature or effect that modifies the die size of your unarmed attacks, that die size instead increases by 1 step, or by 2 steps if you are not wielding a shield or weapon.</p>",
